{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואלה המלכים", :translit "v'eleh ha-melakhim", :gloss "and these are the kings"} {:he "אדוני", :translit "adoni", :gloss "my master"} {:he "מלכו ח' מלכים קודם ישראל", :translit "malkhu khet melakhim kodem yisra'el", :gloss "ruled eight kings before Israel"} {:he "מלכו ח' מלכים עד יהורם", :translit "malkhu khet melakhim ad yehoram", :gloss "ruled eight kings until Jehoram"} {:he "ובימיו פשע אדום", :translit "u-viymav pasha edom", :gloss "and in his days Edom rebelled"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Eightfold verbal repetition of 'adoni' to Esau answered measure-for-measure by eight Edomite kings before any Israelite king"}], :frame {:text "Jacob addresses Esau as 'my master' repeatedly in Genesis 33; tradition counts these occurrences precisely. In the days of Jehoram king of Israel, Edom rebelled, as recorded in 2 Kings 8:20–22. The eight kings of Edom listed in Genesis 36:31–39 correspond to the eight who ruled Israel before that rebellion. The principle of measure-for-measure appears in Mishnah Sotah 1:7 and Megillah 13b, which states that Jacob's deference to Esau gave Esau dominion.", :sources ["Genesis 33" "Genesis 36:31–39" "2 Kings 8:20–22" "Mishnah Sotah 1:7" "Megillah 13b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Eightfold verbal repetition of 'adoni' to Esau answered measure-for-measure by eight Edomite kings before any Israelite king", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:10:11.539435306Z", :model "glm-5.2"}